<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        <a href="/manage/audio-clips">Audio Clips</a> are short recordings played over the kiosk music, such as
        a closing-time call, a birthday jingle or a safety message. The music dips while a clip plays and comes
        back afterwards. Admins, Managers and people with the CanPlayAudioClips role can play them.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="Adding a clip (managers)">
        <ol>
            <li>Select <strong>Add clip</strong> and upload an MP3, WAV or M4A file (up to 25 MB and 5 minutes), or pick one
                already in the File Manager.</li>
            <li>Give it a <strong>Name</strong> and choose where it <strong>Plays at</strong>: one location, or
                <strong>Every location</strong>.</li>
            <li>Set the clip volume. Turn on <strong>Change how the music dips</strong> to set the music level
                while it plays and how quickly it fades down and back up.</li>
        </ol>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Playing a clip now">
        <FluentText>
            Select <strong>Play</strong> on a clip, tick the kiosks, and confirm. You can only play clips on
            kiosks at your own location, and a kiosk needs its location set to play clips.
            <strong>Recently played</strong> shows how each play went: Sent, Getting ready, Playing, Played,
            Stopped, Offline, or Needs update (the kiosk needs a newer version).
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Schedules">
        <FluentText>
            A schedule plays a clip by itself on every kiosk at a location, on the days you tick. Choose
            <strong>Before closing</strong>, <strong>After opening</strong> or <strong>At a set time</strong> (UK time).
            Before closing and after opening use the location's opening hours, so set those on Companies &amp;
            Locations first. A late close after midnight counts as the day before.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
